; MFM auto-recovery: verify filament movement after suspected error
; Called from pause.g while the firmware state is still "pausing" (see there); tool already
; selected, caller is responsible for tool select/deselect
; Sets global.result: 0 = false positive (resume), 1+ = real issue (stay paused)

echo "MFM: starting auto-recovery..."

set global.ignoreMFMevents = true          ; prevent re-triggering during test
M400                                       ; wait for queued moves

; PWM fast-fail is now checked in filament-error.g before pause (standby drops avgPwm)
G90                                        ; absolute mode
G1 X{move.axes[0].min} F60000             ; move to X min for test extrusion
M400

; Reset MFM for a clean measurement
var extruder = 0
M83                                        ; relative extrusion
M591 D{var.extruder} S0                    ; disable
M400
G4 S1
M591 D{var.extruder} A1 S2 E5             ; enable in measurement mode: all moves, 5mm segments (as in print)
M400
G4 S1

; Test extrusion and purge in ONE continuous move. The notch ground into the filament at
; error time sits at the gear; pause.g parks it 13-15mm upstream (G10 retract + 12.5mm), so
; a 15mm test move ends with the gear teeth sitting exactly IN the notch. The earlier layout
; (15mm test, M591 reset at standstill, separate 25mm purge) therefore made the purge start
; from rest with no grip: the test read 105% and the purge collapsed to "gear lost grip" on
; filament that had just fed fine (2026-09-09). While moving, the intact section behind the
; notch carries it across the gear, so do not stop until the ground section is well past it.
; +40mm (-15mm retract below = +25mm net) parks it ~25mm downstream in the guide/melt zone,
; where it just melts through. Slow (1mm/s) so a marginal section is not reground here. The
; MFM measures the whole move: avgPercentage covers the notch crossing (a collapse there
; means the gear lost grip at the notch = real issue), lastPercentage (final 5mm segment)
; proves the filament is still feeding at the end, so a grind that only starts late cannot
; hide behind a good average. Calibration takes the first 10mm; avgPercentage is null until then.
G1 E40 F60                                ; 40mm at 1mm/s
M400
G4 S1

; Evaluate
var avg = sensors.filamentMonitors[var.extruder].avgPercentage
var last = sensors.filamentMonitors[var.extruder].lastPercentage
if var.avg == null || var.last == null
  echo "MFM: auto-recovery — no sensor data"
  set global.result = 1
elif var.avg > 50 && var.last > 50
  echo "MFM: auto-recovery OK (avg " ^ var.avg ^ "%, last " ^ var.last ^ "%) — false positive"
  set global.result = 0
  ; Short suppress window to ride out the resume transient / same off-the-wheel
  ; readings. Both gates (daemon suppress_until AND firmware ignoreMFMevents) are
  ; armed together below so the firmware P=4/P=5 path can't immediately re-pause.
  ; The timestamp set here is only a placeholder: the retract, nozzle clean and the
  ; reheat in resume.g outlast the window, so resume.g re-bases it to the actual
  ; restart of the print (the daemon only evaluates it while "processing").
  set global.mfm_suppress_until = state.upTime + 30
  M220 S100
  set global.mfmbackoff = 3
elif var.avg > 50
  echo "MFM: auto-recovery FAILED (avg " ^ var.avg ^ "%, last " ^ var.last ^ "%) — fed at first, then lost grip: real issue"
  set global.result = 2
else
  echo "MFM: auto-recovery FAILED (avg " ^ var.avg ^ "%, last " ^ var.last ^ "%) — real issue"
  set global.result = 2

; Save recovery result before cleanup (clean.g overwrites global.result)
var recovery_result = global.result

; Retract so the filament state matches what resume.g expects (net +25mm stays)
G1 E-15 F120
M400

; Clean nozzle after test extrusion
G90                                        ; absolute mode
M400
M98 P"0:/sys/meltingplot/nozzle-cleaner/clean.g"

; Restore normal MFM config
M98 P"0:/sys/meltingplot/machine-override"
; On a false positive (result 0) keep events suppressed for the suppress window
; set above — otherwise the same off-the-wheel readings re-trigger filament-error.g
; immediately and loop back into recovery. The daemon clears both ignoreMFMevents
; and mfm_suppress_until when the window expires (daemon.g). On a real issue
; (result != 0) we stay paused, so re-enable events for the operator resume.
if var.recovery_result == 0
  set global.ignoreMFMevents = true
  ; Arm the 30mm distance guard (filament-error.g): a non-null reference is what
  ; enables the guard in the suppression branch. The value itself is re-based by
  ; resume.g after its G11 + re-prime, so the guard measures real print extrusion
  ; since the restart, not the test move or the re-prime.
  set global.mfm_error_extruder_ref = move.extruders[0].position
else
  set global.ignoreMFMevents = false
; Re-snapshot the pause extruder reference: the recovery's own net extrusion (+25mm,
; pass or fail) is system-driven — resume.g must not deduct it from its re-prime (the
; notch parking math above counts on the full 12.7mm feed-forward).
if global.pause_extruder != -1
  set global.pause_extruder_pos = move.extruders[global.pause_extruder].position
  set global.pause_extruder_peak = global.pause_extruder_pos + 12.7
set global.result = var.recovery_result
